1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:00:09,551 --> 00:00:11,553
[♪ tender music playing]

4
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:13,972
How did you get here?

5
00:00:14,056 --> 00:00:15,182
It wasn't too hard on you?

6
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:16,266
[chuckles]

7
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:21,104
Oh!

8
00:00:22,064 --> 00:00:23,774
These stars are beautiful.

9
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:27,402
It gives me courage
looking at them shine like this.

10
00:00:27,486 --> 00:00:29,571
Thank you for your gift, Yubin.

11
00:00:29,655 --> 00:00:30,656
Mm-hmm.

12
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:35,744
[exclaims]

13
00:00:36,328 --> 00:00:37,496
When are you going back?

14
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:39,289
How long can you stay?

15
00:00:39,373 --> 00:00:40,374
[Karin] Hmm?

16
00:00:40,958 --> 00:00:42,084
Hmm.

17
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:44,670
Well, since my goal was
to meet up in person…

18
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:46,547
-Yeah?
-Tomorrow, I think?

19
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:47,923
What?

20
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:49,633
-Tomorrow?
-Oh.

21
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,802
-Is that bad?
-Yeah, it is, because you have to go

22
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:53,345
-on a date with me in Korea.
-Mmm.

23
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:55,264
-Go on a date?
-So you can't leave tomorrow, okay?

24
00:00:55,347 --> 00:00:57,516
-[in Korean] Come on. Let's go.
-[in English] All right, all right.

25
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:59,309
-[in English] Come on, come on.
-[chuckles]

26
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:01,520
[Yubin] What? Tomorrow?

27
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:04,856
WINNER
BEAUTIFUL HOUSE OF THE YEAR

28
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,400
LEE YUBIN

29
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:08,443
EPISODE 7

30
00:01:08,527 --> 00:01:09,528
[door lock beeping]

31
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:12,447
-[in Korean] It's cold. Come on in.
-[Karin, in English] Here?

32
00:01:12,531 --> 00:01:14,449
Ooh.

33
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:15,534
[gasps]

34
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:19,580
Thanks for inviting me to your house.

35
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,459
[in Korean] Whoa, the heater.

36
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:26,003
[heater beeps]

37
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:29,798
[sighs, speaks English] It should
kick on soon. It'll just be a second.

38
00:01:30,549 --> 00:01:32,342
It's all right. I don't mind.

39
00:01:32,426 --> 00:01:34,469
Oh, Karin. Hot cocoa?

40
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:36,805
-[in Korean] Mm-hmm. I'd love that.
-Ah, great.

41
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:37,973
[Karin chuckles]

42
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:03,623
[♪ tender music playing]

43
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:04,708
[chuckles]

44
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:10,130
[gasps]

45
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:23,352
[sighs, chuckles]

46
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:39,534
[chuckles]

47
00:02:42,704 --> 00:02:45,290
[in Korean] All right. There.

48
00:02:46,917 --> 00:02:48,085
Here you go.

49
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:51,380
[in English] Yay, thanks.
This looks so good. Wow.

50
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,841
[blows]

51
00:02:57,386 --> 00:02:58,428
-Hmm.
-Mmm.

52
00:02:58,512 --> 00:03:00,889
-How does it taste?
-[in Korean] Perfect.

53
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:02,349
-Perfect?
-Mm-hmm. [chuckles]

54
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,476
-[chuckles, in English] Oh, I'm glad.
-[chuckles]

55
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:09,147
Mmm.

56
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:13,485
Since I've been gone,
how have things been going in Japan?

57
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:16,446
-Business as usual, I guess.
-Mmm.

58
00:03:16,947 --> 00:03:21,118
Tending to the strawberries,
working in the fields…

59
00:03:22,828 --> 00:03:26,164
Although, doing things alone again
is pretty tough.

60
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:27,499
It's been a while.

61
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:32,003
You missed me, right?

62
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:40,637
I missed the Korean toast
that you used to make me every morning.

63
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,139
You missed me, right?

64
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:45,100
-Your Korean toast is what I missed.
-That's not what I asked.

65
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:47,519
-Hmm?
-Did you miss me or not? Hmm?

66
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:49,104
[chuckling]

67
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:51,064
You didn't miss me at all?

68
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:52,899
Yes, I missed you too.

69
00:03:52,983 --> 00:03:55,152
You're too late. You're too late.
You're too late.

70
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:56,778
-Too late?
-[in Korean] Too late!

71
00:03:56,862 --> 00:03:59,364
[in English] You took too long!
Did you miss me?

72
00:03:59,448 --> 00:04:00,824
I missed you very much.

73
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:02,242
A lot more than I can say.

74
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:04,828
-You aren't lying?
-Of course not.

75
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:07,164
-Hmm.
-And you, Yubin?

76
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,623
Oh, me as well.

77
00:04:08,707 --> 00:04:11,084
I've also missed
the Korean toast that I made.

78
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,086
-What?
-Huh?

79
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:14,880
-[chuckles]
-[chuckles]

80
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,423
I missed you too, all right?

81
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,757
[both laugh]

82
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:19,217
-Lucky me.
-Lucky me.

83
00:04:19,301 --> 00:04:20,343
[Yubin laughs]

84
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:23,180
-[Karin] That thing is so pretty.
-Wow. Pretty.

85
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,681
-Mmm.
-Mm-hmm.

86
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,058
That "thing" is a whale.

87
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:29,853
-Yeah, that thing is pretty.
-Yeah. That "thing."

88
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:32,022
-What?
-It's not "pretty."

89
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:34,816
-That's not pretty?
-Not "pretty." "Whale."

90
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:36,568
Huh?

91
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:38,195
-You're saying it's "pretty?"
-Mmm.

92
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:39,321
It's a whale.

93
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,031
[both laugh]

94
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:42,365
Oh, wait. Do you mean in Korean?

95
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:44,159
-Yeah, in Korean. "That thing."
-"That thing."

96
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:45,243
-It means…
-It means

97
00:04:45,327 --> 00:04:46,703
-a whale. Yeah.
-…a whale?

98
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:48,455
-What?
-Those words sound alike.

99
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:49,706
-Oh, really?
-Mm-hmm.

100
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:53,251
-No way. "Whale" is the same word?
-Yeah, "that thing" means "whale."

101
00:04:53,335 --> 00:04:55,337
-[laughing]
-Ah. [laughing]

102
00:04:57,672 --> 00:04:59,216
-The second time was…
-Mm-hmm.

103
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:01,927
-…the other day, I think?
-Oh. Oh, yeah?

104
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:06,306
[Karin] Lucky me, lucky me.

105
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:10,727
Everybody on Charo Island are doing well.

106
00:05:11,812 --> 00:05:13,647
[gasps] Right! Grandma Hana…

107
00:05:16,358 --> 00:05:17,400
Hmm?

108
00:05:17,484 --> 00:05:19,236
[chuckles softly]

109
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:21,238
Sleeping?

110
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:23,782
[chuckles]

111
00:05:34,209 --> 00:05:35,627
Good night, Yubin.

112
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:32,434
[moans]

113
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:38,648
Yubin.

114
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:42,027
Karin.

115
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:43,945
[Karin] Mmm.

116
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:46,823
[Yubin] Hmm?

117
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:54,205
Will you be my girlfriend?

118
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:58,168
[Karin] Mmm. Mm-hmm.

119
00:06:59,169 --> 00:07:00,170
[Yubin] Mm-hmm?

120
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:10,388
-Hmm?
-[Karin] Hmm?

121
00:07:10,472 --> 00:07:11,681
Hmm?

122
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:14,976
-Huh?
-Huh?

123
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:18,813
Wait. What did you say?

124
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:21,483
What… What did I just say?

125
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:24,694
I asked if you would be my girlfriend.

126
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:29,407
[stammers]

127
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:32,494
[clears throat]

128
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:34,704
Yes.

129
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:37,123
-[sighs, laughing]
-[laughing]

130
00:07:37,791 --> 00:07:40,335
I'm really looking forward
to being your girlfriend.

131
00:07:42,045 --> 00:07:43,463
-[chuckles]
-[Yubin grunts]

132
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,466
I'm really looking forward
to being your boyfriend.

133
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:48,093
-You mean it?
-Yeah.

134
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:52,847
Ask me again.

135
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:56,685
-Will you be my girlfriend?
-[giggling]

136
00:08:00,522 --> 00:08:02,899
-[squeals, laughing]
-[laughing]

137
00:08:04,442 --> 00:08:06,861
-[Yubin] This river is called Hangang.
-[Karin] Mm-hmm?

138
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:08,697
-Hangang?
-Uh-huh.

139
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,365
-I've seen photos of it.
-Mmm.

140
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:13,451
[in Korean] I'm hungry.

141
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:15,286
-You're hungry?
-Mm-hmm.

142
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:16,371
Uh…

143
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:20,083
-[in English] What do you want to eat?
-Hmm…

144
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,168
<i>Tteokbokki!</i>

145
00:08:22,252 --> 00:08:24,003
<i>-Tteokbokki?</i>
-Yeah. I want that.

146
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:25,296
-The spicy kind.
<i>-Tteokbokki?</i>

147
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,757
-What's wrong with that?
-[sighs, speaks Korean] It's pretty spicy.

148
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:30,719
-[Yubin] All right.
-[Karin, in English] Wow.

149
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:32,595
[Yubin, in Korean] Thank you.

150
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:38,685
-Mmm.
-[in English] Is it okay?

151
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:39,936
[in Korean] How is it?

152
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:41,312
[in English] Is it hot?

153
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:44,441
-[in Korean] Is it spicy? It is, isn't it?
-[in English] Yeah, it's so spicy. [yelps]

154
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:46,985
-[groans]
-[in Korean] Here.

155
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,069
JJEONGIGA TTEOKBOKKI

156
00:08:48,153 --> 00:08:49,195
[Karin, in English] So spicy!

157
00:08:50,822 --> 00:08:52,115
-Hot. [grunts]
-[Yubin chuckles]

158
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,199
Is it all right?

159
00:08:53,283 --> 00:08:54,743
-Mmm. It's so good.
-Mm-hmm.

160
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:55,994
-Is it good?
-Mm-hmm.

161
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:57,412
[Yubin, in Korean] Check this out.

162
00:08:58,705 --> 00:08:59,998
[in English] Thank you.

163
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,125
-[in Korean] You go like this…
-Mmm.

164
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:03,835
-[in English] How is it?
-Mmm.

165
00:09:04,419 --> 00:09:06,212
-It's good.
-Mmm.

166
00:09:06,296 --> 00:09:08,006
-[in Korean] It's good.
-It's good? You like it, right?

167
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:10,467
-[in English] Now that we're full of food…
-Mm-hmm.

168
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,760
…it's time to work it off.

169
00:09:11,843 --> 00:09:13,970
-[sucks teeth] All right. Whoever wins…
-Yeah. Uh-huh.

170
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:15,555
…gets their wish granted by the loser.

171
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:17,140
-Okay. [in Korean] Let's go!
-[in English] Okay?

172
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:19,225
[♪ upbeat music playing]

173
00:09:23,188 --> 00:09:24,189
Whoa!

174
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:27,067
-Whoa.
-[Karin chuckles]

175
00:09:37,702 --> 00:09:38,787
[sighs]

176
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:41,664
[Karin] Time's up.

177
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:43,374
[in Korean] How are you so good at this?

178
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,261
Ready?

179
00:09:57,347 --> 00:09:58,848
[Yubin] Whoa, whoa. Oh!

180
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:01,226
-[chuckles]
-[exclaims]

181
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:03,853
-[air hockey table chimes]
-[in English] Okay!

182
00:10:05,188 --> 00:10:06,940
Yay! [giggling]

183
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:08,650
Yeah! Yeah! [laughs]

184
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,194
-[air hockey table chimes]
-Yeah!

185
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:14,322
[sucks teeth] Let's see.

186
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:18,451
Since you're the winner,
I guess you get to make a wish.

187
00:10:18,535 --> 00:10:19,536
-I get the wish?
-Go ahead.

188
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:20,829
-Okay.
-What is it?

189
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,373
Hmm. What do I wish?

190
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,458
Let me think…

191
00:10:25,542 --> 00:10:26,543
[Yubin] Mmm.

192
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:28,670
That, over there.

193
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:30,296
-Let's go in there.
-Huh? That store?

194
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,923
-Yeah, that one.
-Oh, all right.

195
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:34,717
[gasps]

196
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:36,052
Look at this!

197
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:39,639
-Oh, it's cute.
-Oh, wow.

198
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,141
-Yeah, it's cute.
-Mmm.

199
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:44,060
-Oh!
-[Karin] Oh.

200
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:45,812
-It's a bug.
-That's a caterpillar.

201
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:48,148
-Uh-huh.
-[in Korean] Aw, it's so cute! [chuckles]

202
00:10:48,231 --> 00:10:49,524
-[in English] Wait.
-Huh?

203
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:51,818
-[elongated] Oh.
-What?

204
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:52,902
Spitting image.

205
00:10:52,986 --> 00:10:54,946
-That thing?
-It's your twin. [laughing]

206
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:57,240
[in Korean] What'd you say?
[scoffs, chuckles]

207
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,325
-[in English] Yeah. You look alike.
-We do not!

208
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:01,494
What the heck?

209
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:04,873
[in Korean] Let's get these two.

210
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:05,957
-Mm-hmm.
-All right.

211
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,584
-[in English] Ah. Wait a sec.
-Hmm?

212
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,464
Let's match, okay?

213
00:11:13,548 --> 00:11:14,549
Mmm.

214
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:16,217
I've always wanted to try this…

215
00:11:16,301 --> 00:11:17,594
[in Korean] …with a boyfriend.

216
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:21,014
-[in English] We're a couple?
-Mm-hmm. We're a couple.

217
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:24,809
Okay, from now on,
we'll be known as "the bug couple."

218
00:11:24,893 --> 00:11:26,436
-"The bug couple"?
-Yeah.

219
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,520
No, thanks.

220
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:29,189
We're "the <i>ttalgi</i> couple."
Strawberry couple.

221
00:11:29,272 --> 00:11:30,356
[singsongy] Mm-mmm.

222
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,233
-Bugs. Bugs are much cuter.
-[in Korean] Strawberry.

223
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,318
[in English] I wanna be "the bug couple."

224
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:35,570
-Strawberries are way cuter though.
-Mm-mmm, mm-mmm.

225
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,198
-Bugs, bugs, bugs.
-Hey, not "the bug couple."

226
00:11:39,657 --> 00:11:41,576
[electronic voice, in Korean] <i>Two, one…</i>

227
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:42,660
[camera shuttering]

228
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,418
[in English] It's ready.

229
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:51,836
Ah, <i>ramyeon.</i>

230
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,671
Here. [hums]

231
00:11:53,755 --> 00:11:55,256
-[exclaims]
-[chuckles]

232
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:58,134
-I saw Hangang River <i>ramyeon</i> online.
-Mmm.

233
00:11:58,885 --> 00:11:59,886
It's time to eat.

234
00:11:59,969 --> 00:12:01,512
-[in Korean] Let's dig in.
-Okay.

235
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:09,395
-[in English] Well?
-Mmm. Mmm!

236
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:11,022
-You like it?
-[in Korean] Mm-hmm. So good!

237
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,273
Mmm.

238
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:18,613
[in English] Is it done?

239
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:22,992
-[Yubin sighs]
-[chuckles]

240
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:24,202
Thank you.

241
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:25,286
Mmm.

242
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:28,081
Yubin, I had so much fun today.

243
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:31,501
Ah, I'm so glad.
It was a great day, wasn't it?

244
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:32,710
-It really was.
-Mm-hmm.

245
00:12:32,794 --> 00:12:34,712
What about tomorrow?

246
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:36,714
Is there anywhere you have in mind?

247
00:12:36,798 --> 00:12:38,716
Uh, anywhere?

248
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,385
Mm-hmm. Anywhere.

249
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:44,514
Um… [exhales sharply]

250
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:50,103
Uh…

251
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:52,689
Mm-hmm.

252
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:55,566
There is.

253
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,211
Here we are.

254
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,633
THE TREE OF LEE GYEONGSU

255
00:13:22,135 --> 00:13:24,554
"Lee Gyeongsu."

256
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:29,100
Mm-hmm.

257
00:13:30,393 --> 00:13:32,645
Lee Gyeongsu… he was my dad.

258
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:39,652
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

259
00:13:39,736 --> 00:13:40,737
Really?

260
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:41,821
Mm-hmm.

261
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:44,323
Lee Gyeongsu was your dad?

262
00:13:44,407 --> 00:13:45,408
Mm-hmm.

263
00:13:54,876 --> 00:13:55,877
Then…

264
00:13:58,129 --> 00:14:00,214
that figurine I've been keeping safe…

265
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:07,597
[sighs]

266
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:13,644
Now I get it.

267
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:24,530
[in Korean] Long time no see.

268
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:27,992
[in English] …Mr. Gyeongsu, sir.

269
00:14:30,536 --> 00:14:31,704
[in Korean] It's been a while,

270
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,457
Father.

271
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:37,835
Dad.

272
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:38,961
Yeah?

273
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:42,090
Don't you ever get tired
of studying like that all the time?

274
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:43,174
STRAWBERRY

275
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:45,593
Of course I do.

276
00:14:46,761 --> 00:14:48,346
But I enjoy it.

277
00:14:50,056 --> 00:14:52,809
It's hard, but you enjoy it?

278
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:56,062
What do you enjoy doing, Yubin?

279
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:59,690
You like drawing.

280
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:01,984
You're good with your hands,
just like your mom.

281
00:15:02,068 --> 00:15:03,069
[scoffs]

282
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:06,447
Mine are just doodling.

283
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:18,709
Did you draw this?

284
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:23,464
-Give it back!
-Wow, that is amazing.

285
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:29,554
We should build our house
like this someday.

286
00:15:33,432 --> 00:15:35,601
It'd be perfect if there was a tree here.

287
00:15:36,519 --> 00:15:38,646
I could sit in its shade
and read a book with your mom.

288
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:42,859
[scoffs] We don't need a tree.

289
00:15:43,442 --> 00:15:44,902
-I'll draw one myself.
-Huh?

290
00:15:44,986 --> 00:15:49,157
-Wait. Hey. Let me do it.
-What? I can do it.

291
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,783
I know how to draw too!

292
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:51,993
You're going to ruin it.

293
00:15:52,869 --> 00:15:54,370
Draw it over here then.

294
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:57,456
What kind of tree do you want?

295
00:15:58,124 --> 00:16:00,042
Hmm? A big,

296
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,128
nice tree.

297
00:16:04,589 --> 00:16:05,882
A long-living tree.

298
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:14,223
Like a huge 100-year-old tree.

299
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:18,644
[inhales sharply, chuckles]
You sketched that so fast.

300
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:22,148
It's incredible.

301
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:26,527
The room under the tree is mine.

302
00:16:26,611 --> 00:16:28,446
No, this one's for Mom.

303
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:31,324
Yours is this one.

304
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:33,826
-[chuckles] Bring Mom here.
-[chuckles]

305
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:37,163
[Gyeongsu] <i>Mom and I will share the room.</i>
[chuckles]

306
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:06,484
[Yubin] All done.

307
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:13,199
Ooh.

308
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,160
[in English]
I didn't realize I was this hungry.

309
00:17:16,786 --> 00:17:19,163
-Ooh. That looks fantastic.
-[chuckles] Mmm.

310
00:17:19,789 --> 00:17:21,791
-It's <i>doenjang jjigae.</i>
<i>-Doenjang jjigae?</i>

311
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:23,084
-[Yubin] Right.
-Yum.

312
00:17:24,669 --> 00:17:25,920
[sighs]

313
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:27,922
-[phone buzzing]
-[Karin] Hmm?

314
00:17:28,005 --> 00:17:30,716
MR. KUROKAWA

315
00:17:31,926 --> 00:17:34,554
Sorry, Yubin.
This will only take a minute.

316
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:35,638
Sure.

317
00:17:42,270 --> 00:17:45,064
[whispers] Okay, okay, okay.

318
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,109
Karin speaking.

319
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,819
Oh, Karin, hi.

320
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:53,364
I'm checking in to see if you've thought
about our talk from the other day.

321
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,075
Uh…

322
00:17:57,118 --> 00:18:01,539
If you remember, I proposed
we distribute your berries nationwide.

323
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:04,542
<i>Right. It's, uh…</i>

324
00:18:06,252 --> 00:18:09,964
It's just… I'm not sure
if the quality'd be maintainable.

325
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:15,845
That's a large number of strawberries
to be growing like that in my open field.

326
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,430
I'm a little worried about it.

327
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:24,270
With Green Nova Corporation's
cutting-edge technology,

328
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:27,481
we'll definitely be able
to ensure some degree of quality.

329
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:31,319
Some degree of quality?

330
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:32,403
Right.

331
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:37,783
You know I understand your dedication
to preserving top-notch quality.

332
00:18:38,409 --> 00:18:42,038
However, remember that choosing one thing

333
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:46,167
often means that another thing
will inevitably fall to the wayside.

334
00:18:46,751 --> 00:18:47,835
Right.

335
00:18:47,918 --> 00:18:50,838
<i>But listen,</i>
<i>there's nothing for you to worry about</i>

336
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:54,008
<i>with those wonderful strawberries</i>
<i>that you've developed.</i>

337
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:57,011
How about I email you the proposal,
for now?

338
00:18:57,595 --> 00:19:01,015
Or if you prefer, we can chat
at Green Nova Corporation's office

339
00:19:01,098 --> 00:19:02,642
in the coming few days.

340
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:07,688
All right. [sighs]

341
00:19:09,899 --> 00:19:11,233
I appreciate the offer.

342
00:19:12,652 --> 00:19:14,654
I'll reach out in the next few days.

343
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:18,199
I will.

344
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,493
Have a good night, sir.

345
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,173
[sighs]

346
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,476
Uh, Yubin?

347
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:50,356
Yubin?

348
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:52,775
-[Yubin] Ta-da!
-Oh.

349
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:55,236
[chuckles] It's your birthday celebration.

350
00:19:56,821 --> 00:19:58,197
What? [chuckles]

351
00:19:58,948 --> 00:20:00,783
-[in Korean] All right.
-[chuckles]

352
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:03,494
Come on, over here. Right this way.

353
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:04,620
[Karin chuckles]

354
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:06,539
[in English] Wow.

355
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:08,499
KARIN
HAPPY BIRTHDAY

356
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:11,627
[in Korean] Ah, here you go. Put this on.

357
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:14,004
Ah, there.

358
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:15,673
[chuckles]

359
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:17,425
[in English] Make a wish.
Blow out the candles.

360
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:19,385
-It's wish time? Hmm.
-Put your hands like this.

361
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:29,145
[Karin chuckles]

362
00:20:29,854 --> 00:20:31,814
-[in Korean] Thank you so much.
-[chuckles]

363
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:33,274
[in English] Thanks for being born.

364
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:38,237
-Let's have some cake.
-Okay.

365
00:20:40,406 --> 00:20:42,408
-Wow, these are cute.
-Oh, they're cute?

366
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:44,285
-They're adorable.
-Which do you like more?

367
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:45,536
-Which one?
-What? All of 'em.

368
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:47,455
-You like them all? Oh.
-This one, this one, this one.

369
00:20:47,538 --> 00:20:48,831
-Want a bite?
-No, thanks.

370
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:53,836
[in Korean] Here you go…

371
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:56,464
-[in English] Thank you, sir.
-[grunts]

372
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,974
[♪ tender music playing]

373
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:15,858
Is there something on your mind?

374
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:16,942
[Karin] Hmm?

375
00:21:19,445 --> 00:21:20,446
Hmm…

376
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:25,534
I think that…

377
00:21:27,495 --> 00:21:30,039
I should head back to Japan tomorrow.

378
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:37,463
[Yubin inhales deeply, sighs]

379
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:41,842
I get it.

380
00:21:47,515 --> 00:21:50,184
I would love to stay here with you
a little longer,

381
00:21:52,645 --> 00:21:55,022
but I need
to take care of my strawberries.

382
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:58,359
I came here spontaneously.

383
00:21:59,568 --> 00:22:00,986
Well, when you get back,

384
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:05,616
will you promise
you'll think about me a lot?

385
00:22:08,953 --> 00:22:10,037
Mm-hmm.

386
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:11,664
-Oh, will you?
-Mm-hmm.

387
00:22:11,747 --> 00:22:14,083
Of course I will. I'll think about you.

388
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:16,460
[chuckles]

389
00:22:20,714 --> 00:22:22,675
-[chuckles]
-[sighs]

390
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:27,930
[Karin sighs]

391
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:34,395
KUROKAWA

392
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:47,825
-[footsteps approaching]
-[secretary] Excuse me, Director.

393
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:49,451
Yes?

394
00:22:51,662 --> 00:22:52,663
Director,

395
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:56,041
I've brought additional samples
of Shirahama Karin's strawberries

396
00:22:56,125 --> 00:22:57,459
-as you requested.
-Ah.

397
00:22:57,543 --> 00:22:59,628
Hurry.
Measure the strawberry samples' sweetness.

398
00:22:59,712 --> 00:23:00,713
Yes, sir.

399
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:05,050
[♪ quirky music playing]

400
00:23:05,134 --> 00:23:06,135
[sucks teeth]

401
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:08,095
Hmm…

402
00:23:10,848 --> 00:23:13,017
-Ugh. Never mind. Move aside.
-[gasps]

403
00:23:52,431 --> 00:23:53,766
[beeps]

404
00:23:57,561 --> 00:23:59,647
Oh, their sweetness has evolved.

405
00:24:00,773 --> 00:24:02,316
With its quality,

406
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:03,943
the strawberries can hold their own

407
00:24:04,026 --> 00:24:06,445
amongst Green Nova Corporation's
popular products.

408
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:08,030
In the premium lineup, no doubt.

409
00:24:14,036 --> 00:24:17,247
This variety could be
the future of our company.

410
00:24:28,384 --> 00:24:29,718
[sighs heavily]

411
00:24:30,469 --> 00:24:33,389
[Mari] Karin is gone and Yubin is gone…

412
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:38,268
And Kunam is gone too.

413
00:24:40,354 --> 00:24:41,855
[phone buzzes]

414
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:47,027
[Karin] <i>I'm at the airport.</i>

415
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:49,071
[sighs]

416
00:24:50,364 --> 00:24:51,949
Looks like she made it back all right.

417
00:24:57,579 --> 00:25:00,082
[♪ mystical music plays]

418
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:08,882
[sighs]

419
00:25:20,519 --> 00:25:21,770
Tell me, cards…

420
00:25:23,439 --> 00:25:25,441
what does fate have in store for us?

421
00:25:27,276 --> 00:25:28,402
[sighs]

422
00:25:55,345 --> 00:25:57,097
[exhales deeply]

423
00:26:00,934 --> 00:26:03,353
[thunderclap, rumbling]

424
00:26:04,063 --> 00:26:05,272
Does this mean…

425
00:26:06,231 --> 00:26:07,941
a crumbling heart?

426
00:26:09,068 --> 00:26:11,278
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

427
00:26:15,365 --> 00:26:16,366
[gasps]

428
00:26:16,450 --> 00:26:17,451
[sinister laugh]

429
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:19,620
Could this mean "temptation"?

430
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:22,956
No way. Is Kunam seeing another woman?

431
00:26:36,345 --> 00:26:37,930
[♪ ominous music playing]

432
00:26:38,013 --> 00:26:39,264
[gasps]

433
00:26:40,557 --> 00:26:42,935
-[swords clanking]
-[gasps, whimpers]

434
00:26:43,018 --> 00:26:44,603
Anything but that!

435
00:26:44,686 --> 00:26:46,855
Dear tarot cards,
this can't be my destiny!

436
00:26:46,939 --> 00:26:50,859
Oh, please,
please change your mind! [sobs]

437
00:26:50,943 --> 00:26:52,277
-[vehicle approaching]
-[gasps]

438
00:26:52,361 --> 00:26:53,737
-Kunam?
-[engine shuts off]

439
00:26:59,409 --> 00:27:00,744
[sighs]

440
00:27:00,828 --> 00:27:02,830
Oh. Hi, Mari.

441
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:06,500
-Hi, Grandpa Asahi.
-It's nice to see you.

442
00:27:15,217 --> 00:27:16,677
-Are you looking for something?
-Ah.

443
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:18,512
Uh… It's… right here.

444
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:20,556
-Curry powder. I ran out earlier.
-Oh!

445
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:21,640
[both chuckle]

446
00:27:21,723 --> 00:27:23,350
I'll ring you up over here.

447
00:27:30,858 --> 00:27:32,025
[register beeping]

448
00:27:33,944 --> 00:27:38,031
Grandpa Asahi, you've haven't
seen Kunam around lately, have you?

449
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:41,368
-Has it been a while?
-Yeah.

450
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:43,829
Well, he's been pretty busy, you know.

451
00:27:43,912 --> 00:27:45,330
[scoffs]

452
00:27:45,414 --> 00:27:47,207
Oh, yeah? What's he been so busy with?

453
00:27:47,291 --> 00:27:49,209
Chasing after a bunch of women?

454
00:27:49,293 --> 00:27:51,211
Mari, he's got you, right?

455
00:27:51,295 --> 00:27:53,463
He's not chasing other girls.

456
00:27:53,547 --> 00:27:57,301
Well, what he told me
is that he's been job-hunting.

457
00:27:57,384 --> 00:27:58,677
What?

458
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:01,305
Wait, I thought he was happy working here.
Wasn't he?

459
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:06,226
Yes, but he said that just working here
doesn't qualify towards a work visa.

460
00:28:07,185 --> 00:28:09,521
That's why he's been busy
pounding the pavement,

461
00:28:09,605 --> 00:28:11,356
looking for qualifying employment.

462
00:28:12,065 --> 00:28:13,859
[Kunam] Sorry to do this out of the blue.

463
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:15,611
Ah, no, I understand.

464
00:28:16,445 --> 00:28:17,696
Go on.

465
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:20,949
I think that we should take a break.

466
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:22,409
[exclaims]

467
00:28:25,954 --> 00:28:26,955
What the heck?

468
00:28:27,039 --> 00:28:30,292
He always shows up no matter what,
even if I tell him not to come here.

469
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:32,711
He can't even bother to say hi?

470
00:28:35,255 --> 00:28:37,841
It's all beginning to make sense now.

471
00:28:38,675 --> 00:28:41,511
[Asahi] He came to Charo Island
to visit and explore,

472
00:28:41,595 --> 00:28:44,348
but then he ended up staying here.

473
00:28:44,431 --> 00:28:45,599
It must've caught up to him

474
00:28:45,682 --> 00:28:48,518
because he didn't think
to prepare for a work visa.

475
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:53,273
Uh, excuse me…
I think that I'm a little lost.

476
00:28:53,774 --> 00:28:57,027
Do you happen to know
where I can find the ferry terminal?

477
00:28:57,611 --> 00:28:58,779
It's that way.

478
00:29:00,030 --> 00:29:02,324
But you'll never make it
before they leave the port.

479
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:04,701
Then, when will the next ferry arrive?

480
00:29:04,785 --> 00:29:06,161
Not for another two hours.

481
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:07,579
Two hours…

482
00:29:08,205 --> 00:29:09,206
[groans]

483
00:29:09,790 --> 00:29:11,333
-[sighs]
-[chuckles]

484
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:12,834
[♪ whimsical music playing]

485
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:15,087
Do you wanna sit down?

486
00:29:15,796 --> 00:29:16,797
[in Korean] Sorry?

487
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,882
[in English]
Your legs look tired from walking around.

488
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:22,844
Thanks.

489
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:27,140
[Mari] Mmm.

490
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:31,645
Oh, thank you so much.

491
00:29:35,607 --> 00:29:40,153
As a tourist or traveler or whatever,
you're just wandering around anyway.

492
00:29:40,821 --> 00:29:43,740
You don't need to be so precious
about sticking to a schedule.

493
00:29:43,824 --> 00:29:45,826
[♪ music continues]

494
00:29:54,418 --> 00:29:55,419
[Kunam, in Korean] Wow…

495
00:29:57,004 --> 00:29:58,588
[chuckles]

496
00:30:02,676 --> 00:30:06,346
[in English] This seat right here
has the best view on Charo island.

497
00:30:16,398 --> 00:30:18,150
Um, could…

498
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:20,277
I stay here…

499
00:30:20,360 --> 00:30:22,779
uh, a little while longer?

500
00:30:23,572 --> 00:30:25,240
Not just for two hours?

501
00:30:25,323 --> 00:30:26,491
[chuckles]

502
00:30:27,284 --> 00:30:29,953
Do what you want. Why are you asking me?

503
00:30:30,037 --> 00:30:32,164
Don't cause trouble
while you're here, all right?

504
00:30:41,006 --> 00:30:42,507
Good morning!

505
00:30:47,929 --> 00:30:49,306
[in Korean] All right.

506
00:30:53,643 --> 00:30:57,189
[in English] Um, I just started
working over there! Right over there.

507
00:30:57,272 --> 00:30:58,273
[chuckles]

508
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:00,942
Don't cause any trouble, got it?

509
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:02,778
Uh, one more thing.

510
00:31:03,403 --> 00:31:06,156
My name is Park Kunam.

511
00:31:08,408 --> 00:31:11,119
It's nice to meet you, then.
I'm Mizuno Mari.

512
00:31:11,203 --> 00:31:12,370
Mari…

513
00:31:13,038 --> 00:31:14,206
Mizuno Mari…

514
00:31:15,665 --> 00:31:18,168
Mari, I'm so happy to meet you.

515
00:31:18,251 --> 00:31:20,253
[♪ sentimental music playing]

516
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:28,303
[music ends]

517
00:31:30,931 --> 00:31:32,933
[alarm beeping]

518
00:31:35,644 --> 00:31:37,104
-[groans]
-[phone chimes]

519
00:31:42,067 --> 00:31:43,610
[Yubin, in Korean] <i>Good morning, Karin.</i>

520
00:31:43,693 --> 00:31:45,445
<i>I just got up.</i>

521
00:31:45,529 --> 00:31:46,780
[in English] Morning.

522
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:49,741
[♪ whimsical music playing]

523
00:31:53,411 --> 00:31:55,956
<i>Good morning, Yubin. You're an early bird.</i>

524
00:31:56,039 --> 00:31:57,040
[Yubin, in Korean] <i>Yeah.</i>

525
00:31:58,792 --> 00:32:01,169
-[Karin, in English] <i>What are you doing?</i>
-[in Korean] <i>Just zoning out.</i>

526
00:32:01,837 --> 00:32:03,171
[chuckles]

527
00:32:05,215 --> 00:32:07,801
-[phone buzzes]
-Which should I go with?

528
00:32:09,427 --> 00:32:11,429
This one?

529
00:32:14,474 --> 00:32:15,475
Or this one?

530
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:20,939
[shutter clicks]

531
00:32:23,567 --> 00:32:24,568
[shutter clicks]

532
00:32:24,651 --> 00:32:26,945
-[phone chimes]
-[Karin] Hmm?

533
00:32:30,407 --> 00:32:31,783
[Yubin] <i>Which do you like better?</i>

534
00:32:33,243 --> 00:32:34,494
[Karin] Hmm.

535
00:32:39,291 --> 00:32:42,335
[in English] <i>Hmm… I like the first one!</i>

536
00:32:44,379 --> 00:32:47,048
[in Korean] The first one. Okay.

537
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:50,594
[food sizzling]

538
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:55,473
[in English] Hot, hot… ugh. [yelps]

539
00:32:57,684 --> 00:32:59,227
Did I make it right?

540
00:32:59,311 --> 00:33:03,857
It kind of looks different
from the toast you made before…

541
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:04,941
[phone buzzes]

542
00:33:05,442 --> 00:33:06,568
[Yubin] Hmm.

543
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:07,652
[Karin] <i>Did I make it right?</i>

544
00:33:07,736 --> 00:33:09,988
<i>It kind of looks different</i>
<i>from the toast you made before…</i>

545
00:33:10,071 --> 00:33:15,410
[in Korean]
You can be more generous with the sugar.

546
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:18,246
<i>You can be more generous with the sugar.</i>

547
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:20,999
[in English] More generous?

548
00:33:21,875 --> 00:33:22,959
How much should I add?

549
00:33:23,919 --> 00:33:28,506
[in Korean] As much as you miss me.

550
00:33:29,758 --> 00:33:31,468
<i>As much as you miss me.</i>

551
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:32,552
[Karin chortles]

552
00:33:33,220 --> 00:33:35,222
[♪ whimsical music continues]

553
00:33:44,564 --> 00:33:45,774
[sighing] Ah…

554
00:33:45,857 --> 00:33:47,275
She misses me a lot.

555
00:33:56,826 --> 00:33:57,827
[music ends]

556
00:34:03,625 --> 00:34:05,710
[pages flipping]

557
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:19,224
-[clipboard thuds]
-[sighs]

558
00:34:35,031 --> 00:34:39,411
Which team manages
the bio-based building materials?

559
00:34:41,621 --> 00:34:43,290
I need an explanation.

560
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:48,378
You got residents to sign consent forms
before the project even kicked off.

561
00:34:49,296 --> 00:34:51,715
Most of them are elderly residents too.

562
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:56,678
[chuckles] Mr. Lee,
I wish you'd see the bigger picture here.

563
00:34:56,761 --> 00:34:58,847
It's better to clear off some farmland

564
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:02,642
if it means revitalizing
the whole village.

565
00:35:03,268 --> 00:35:04,519
Besides,

566
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:08,106
we'll pay a generous compensation
to the residents.

567
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:09,357
Compensation?

568
00:35:10,483 --> 00:35:14,237
It's not just some land.

569
00:35:14,321 --> 00:35:16,698
It's the residents' way of life.

570
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:19,534
How many times do I have to tell you

571
00:35:19,618 --> 00:35:21,786
that profit is
the company's greatest priority?

572
00:35:21,870 --> 00:35:25,457
Yes, profit is important.

573
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:29,586
You've reported
an estimated profit margin of 12%.

574
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:32,631
I looked into the risk factors.

575
00:35:32,714 --> 00:35:37,093
A 40% risk of delay
due to the farmland's rezoning denial.

576
00:35:37,636 --> 00:35:42,682
15% loss from potential class action suit
if the consent is found to be forged.

577
00:35:42,766 --> 00:35:47,187
The company's image would take a hit
if it is deemed an environmental issue.

578
00:35:47,270 --> 00:35:50,940
There would be a 20% drop
in presale premium.

579
00:35:51,024 --> 00:35:52,734
What do you think about that?

580
00:35:53,485 --> 00:35:54,861
That was the best-case scenario…

581
00:35:54,944 --> 00:35:56,738
And the worst case?

582
00:35:57,238 --> 00:35:58,823
Sir.

583
00:35:59,324 --> 00:36:02,160
If you keep trying to force
this project through,

584
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:04,913
you could end up
bringing the whole company down.

585
00:36:04,996 --> 00:36:07,374
Once we get the approval…

586
00:36:07,457 --> 00:36:08,458
I've already

587
00:36:09,084 --> 00:36:13,129
emailed Legal and Audit divisions

588
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:15,423
about the forged resident consents,

589
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:20,887
and the side contract you made with
a subcontractor behind the company's back.

590
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:22,263
[♪ upbeat music playing]

591
00:36:22,347 --> 00:36:23,431
Sir…

592
00:36:25,141 --> 00:36:26,726
try to see the bigger picture here.

593
00:36:27,936 --> 00:36:34,025
This land could end up
becoming your grave, not a resort.

594
00:36:35,944 --> 00:36:39,489
Wait, Mr. Lee.

595
00:36:39,572 --> 00:36:42,033
I will work with you.

596
00:36:42,117 --> 00:36:44,577
I'll support you every step of the way.

597
00:36:44,661 --> 00:36:49,708
Walking out like this
will mean abandoning your career.

598
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,296
You can have it.

599
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:58,091
My career.

600
00:37:02,303 --> 00:37:03,805
[music ends]

601
00:37:04,806 --> 00:37:05,807
What?

602
00:37:08,101 --> 00:37:09,102
[knocks on door]

603
00:37:14,357 --> 00:37:16,484
You never come see me.

604
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:21,740
[sighs]

605
00:37:29,789 --> 00:37:32,709
LEE YUBIN, PROJECT DIRECTOR

606
00:37:35,587 --> 00:37:37,630
I couldn't meet your expectations.

607
00:37:38,631 --> 00:37:39,632
Sorry.

608
00:37:41,301 --> 00:37:45,096
[sighs] I love this,
so I intended to give it my all…

609
00:37:48,683 --> 00:37:49,976
But this is the end of the line.

610
00:37:52,395 --> 00:37:53,897
You're joking.

611
00:37:55,398 --> 00:37:57,150
You want to blow this chance?

612
00:37:59,110 --> 00:38:01,446
I'm not blowing it. Hmm.

613
00:38:02,989 --> 00:38:04,449
I'm letting it go.

614
00:38:04,532 --> 00:38:06,409
If you are unhappy with the GM's methods,

615
00:38:07,410 --> 00:38:09,120
I can talk to the company.

616
00:38:09,204 --> 00:38:12,540
You're a valuable client.

617
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:15,710
You put your faith in me,
and you're thorough.

618
00:38:17,128 --> 00:38:19,297
Yeah. [sucks teeth]

619
00:38:20,381 --> 00:38:22,300
I may have treated you coldly…

620
00:38:24,803 --> 00:38:27,806
but I always appreciated
how reliable you were.

621
00:38:28,890 --> 00:38:32,644
You should stay
until this project is over. Hmm?

622
00:38:33,228 --> 00:38:35,021
Let this be your last one.

623
00:38:35,104 --> 00:38:37,357
[♪ sentimental music playing]

624
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:39,484
Thank you for trusting me.

625
00:38:41,069 --> 00:38:42,195
But from now on,

626
00:38:42,904 --> 00:38:44,823
I'll get back on my feet on my own.

627
00:38:45,615 --> 00:38:46,741
Sia, I wish you…

628
00:38:48,451 --> 00:38:49,452
the best.

629
00:38:57,627 --> 00:38:58,628
[sighs]

630
00:38:59,462 --> 00:39:02,215
I wish he could've been mean.

631
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:07,220
[sighs] He's the worst.

632
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:12,100
LEE YUBIN, EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR

633
00:39:12,183 --> 00:39:13,184
[music ends]

634
00:39:13,268 --> 00:39:14,269
[sighs]

635
00:39:16,312 --> 00:39:19,232
CHARO ISLAND
NOVEL STRAWBERRY VARIETY

636
00:39:19,315 --> 00:39:22,318
BRAND CONTRACT PROPOSAL

637
00:39:26,739 --> 00:39:27,740
DEAR KARIN SHIRAHAMA,

638
00:39:27,824 --> 00:39:29,200
CONGRATULATIONS
ON TAKING FIRST PLACE

639
00:39:29,284 --> 00:39:30,785
AT GREEN NOVA CORPORATION FESTA.

640
00:39:30,869 --> 00:39:33,079
THESE ARE THE DETAILS
OF THE SPECIAL SUPPORT PROGRAM

641
00:39:33,162 --> 00:39:34,163
AWARDED TO THE WINNER.

642
00:39:35,206 --> 00:39:36,332
[exhales]

643
00:39:45,341 --> 00:39:47,051
[in English] "Pursuant to this agreement,

644
00:39:47,135 --> 00:39:52,223
all rights relating to the crop variety's
development, propagation, distribution,

645
00:39:52,307 --> 00:39:57,604
and secondary use shall be transferred
to the Green Nova Corporation."

646
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:01,524
Does this mean that

647
00:40:02,901 --> 00:40:05,153
they're only commercializing
the crop seed?

648
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:06,821
[phone buzzing]

649
00:40:13,453 --> 00:40:14,454
Karin speaking.

650
00:40:14,996 --> 00:40:17,999
<i>Oh, Ms. Shirahama.</i>
<i>This is Secretary Shioiri,</i>

651
00:40:18,082 --> 00:40:21,961
calling on behalf of Executive Director
Kurokawa of Green Nova Corporation.

652
00:40:22,545 --> 00:40:23,880
[Karin] <i>Hi, thanks for calling.</i>

653
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:25,506
[chuckles]

654
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:27,634
Have you had the chance
to review the contract

655
00:40:27,717 --> 00:40:29,510
in the email we sent the other day?

656
00:40:29,594 --> 00:40:31,054
I'm doing it as we speak.

657
00:40:31,638 --> 00:40:33,598
Oh, that's wonderful to hear.

658
00:40:33,681 --> 00:40:35,642
You have the option
to provide a digital signature.

659
00:40:35,725 --> 00:40:39,395
<i>So I called to lend you my assistance in</i>
<i>walking you through the signing process.</i>

660
00:40:39,479 --> 00:40:40,730
Uh, signing?

661
00:40:42,106 --> 00:40:43,316
I still need to…

662
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:45,652
[stammers] I'm sorry.

663
00:40:46,402 --> 00:40:48,696
I appreciate this offer
and everything you've been doing,

664
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:52,158
but I feel like the current contract

665
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:55,995
doesn't protect my strawberries'
current open-field growing method.

666
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:02,377
Huh? What?

667
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:06,339
Uh, Director Kurokawa informed me you'd
already agreed to signing the contract.

668
00:41:06,923 --> 00:41:08,257
What?

669
00:41:08,341 --> 00:41:10,009
Director Kurokawa?

670
00:41:10,093 --> 00:41:11,427
Uh… Did…

671
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:13,930
he really say I already signed?

672
00:41:15,682 --> 00:41:17,225
<i>-Uh…</i>
-[sighs]

673
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:18,309
<i>That's, um…</i>

674
00:41:18,393 --> 00:41:20,311
Maybe there was a miscommunication.

675
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:23,481
I'm sorry, could you give me
a little more time?

676
00:41:24,273 --> 00:41:25,316
Uh…

677
00:41:26,401 --> 00:41:28,778
Then if you don't mind,
would you give me an estimate

678
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:30,196
on when you'd have an answer?

679
00:41:30,279 --> 00:41:33,658
We were hoping to hear your reply
as soon as possible.

680
00:41:34,993 --> 00:41:35,994
Absolutely.

681
00:41:36,077 --> 00:41:37,328
I'll respond soon.

682
00:41:37,954 --> 00:41:42,750
Um… as soon as I make a choice,
I'll follow up with you via email.

683
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:45,503
Thank you for your patience.

684
00:41:46,754 --> 00:41:47,755
Goodbye, sir.

685
00:41:50,675 --> 00:41:51,718
[sighs]

686
00:41:57,056 --> 00:42:00,059
[♪ ominous music playing]

687
00:42:11,195 --> 00:42:12,196
[music ends]

688
00:42:14,907 --> 00:42:17,410
[♪ gentle music playing]

689
00:42:19,996 --> 00:42:21,164
[Karin sighs]

690
00:42:23,166 --> 00:42:26,085
[Kurokawa] <i>What do you think about</i>
<i>creating a brand for your strawberries?</i>

691
00:42:26,169 --> 00:42:27,712
Creating a brand, sir?

692
00:42:28,296 --> 00:42:29,881
Nationwide distribution.

693
00:42:29,964 --> 00:42:31,966
We could send your berries
throughout Japan.

694
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:36,804
<i>Don't you want more people</i>
<i>to experience your produce?</i>

695
00:42:44,020 --> 00:42:45,480
[voice, in distance] Hey, boss!

696
00:42:50,234 --> 00:42:51,944
Hey, boss!

697
00:42:53,780 --> 00:42:55,782
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

698
00:42:55,865 --> 00:42:57,909
[footsteps echoing]

699
00:43:38,241 --> 00:43:39,242
[groans]

700
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:47,750
Karin.

701
00:43:50,044 --> 00:43:51,045
I'm home.

702
00:43:52,505 --> 00:43:53,840
Welcome back.

703
00:44:17,405 --> 00:44:19,699
MERRY BERRY LOVE

704
00:44:19,782 --> 00:44:20,783
NEXT EPISODE

705
00:44:20,867 --> 00:44:22,410
I'm back to square one.

706
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:24,787
-[Karin] <i>It's a welcome party for you.</i>
-Cheers!

707
00:44:25,746 --> 00:44:29,000
[Kurokawa] <i>Of course…</i>
<i>No wonder he's such an eyesore.</i>
